description:
In app.js handleStateEvent() (lines 555-566), when new messages arrive via EventSource, the code filters them by currentChatId before appending:

  if (result.created && result.created.length > 0 && currentChatId) {
    const getResponses = await callJmap([...]);
    for (const msg of getResult.list) {
      if (msg.chatId === currentChatId) {
        appendMessageBubble(msg);
      }
    }
  }

This prevents a message meant for chat A from appearing in chat B (e.g., if the user switches chats between the push event and fetching the message details).

The check 'chatId === currentChatId' ensures we only render messages for the currently displayed chat, but also updates unread counts for other chats (line 570 refreshes the whole list).

Correct pattern.
